module

public import Feec.Legacy.MirrorCube.Ext

/-!
# Thesis Prop 4.17 on the box `Q = (0, ½)³` with tensorial mirror boundary conditions

**Status.** Part of `Feec.Legacy`, the real-scalar short-complex development (built on
`Feec.Legacy.HilbertComplex2`) that the cube models and some counterexamples still use. It
keeps only what those modules need and the results that have no home in the general layers
yet; everything else moved there (see `docs/migration/map.tsv`).

**Thesis claim** ([QuennevilleBelair2015, §4.10, Prop 4.17, p. 67]). On a bounded contractible
`Ω`, for the complex `H̊¹(V) → H̊(curl, M) → L²(M)`, data `(0, E₀, B₀)` with `E₀`, `B₀` TSD give
a solution of (4.14) with `σ ≡ 0` and `E`, `B` TSD for all time, solving the EB equations; Ch. 7
runs (4.14) numerically on a unit cube mesh.

**Defect.** With these boundary conditions the projection hypothesis and the conclusion fail on
every bounded domain (`Feec.Legacy.BoundedDomain.thesisComplex_tsd_not_propagates`), and
on every open cube only stationary TSD data propagate (`Feec.Legacy.BoxIdent.openCube_forward_iff`).
`Feec.Legacy.Box.Mirror` repairs the statement for tensorial mirror boundary conditions, but only in
the parity model on `ℓ²(ℤ³)`.

**Repair (this file).** A Hilbert complex of genuine fields on `Q`,
`mirrorCxQ : L²(Q; ℝ³) → L²(Q; ℝ³ˣ³) → L²(Q; ℝ³ˣ³)`, for which Prop 4.17 holds with existence,
uniqueness, `K* = K` and non-stationary TSD data. It is the compression
(`Feec.Legacy.MirrorCube.comprComplex`) of the periodic complex of `Feec.Legacy.Torus.Basic` by the mirror
extensions `Jv`, `Jm 1`, `Jm (-1)` of `Feec.Legacy.MirrorCube.Ext`:
* `D(d0) = {σ ∈ L²(Q; ℝ³) : Jv σ ∈ H¹(𝕋³)}`, `d0 σ = (grad Jv σ)|_Q`: the weak gradient on `Q`
  (`mirrorCxQ_d0_weakGrad`); the boundary condition is `σ · n = 0` (`σ_a` odd in `x_a`);
* `D(d1) = {E : Jm₁ E ∈ H(curl, 𝕋³)}`, `d1 E = (curl Jm₁ E)|_Q`: the weak curl on `Q`
  (`mirrorCxQ_d1_eq`, `D(d1) ⊆ H(curl, Q)`); the boundary condition is `E_{nτ} = 0`
  (the entries `E_{nτ}` are odd in the normal variable);
* the adjoints are the weak `-div` and the weak curl on `Q` (`mirrorCxQ_adj0_eq`,
  `mirrorCxQ_adj1_eq`), with the complementary conditions `E_{τn} = 0` for `D(d0*)` and
  `B_{ττ} = 0` for `D(d1*)`.
Here a boundary condition "`f = 0` on the face `x_i ∈ {0, ½}`" is encoded by the method of
images: the extension of `f` to `𝕋³ = ℝ³/ℤ³` that is odd in `x_i` has the required Sobolev
regularity across the face. This is the reflection characterization of the trace condition for
flat faces; a trace-theoretic definition on `Q` is not formalized. In the other direction,
`H̊¹(Q) ⊆ D(d0)` and `H̊(curl, Q) ⊆ D(d1)` are proved in `Feec.Legacy.MirrorCube.CubeDense`.

The constraint spaces are `TSDmE = Jm₁⁻¹ L²(TSD)(𝕋³)`, `TSDmB = Jm₋₁⁻¹ L²(TSD)(𝕋³)`: fields in
`L²(TSD)(Q)` (`TSDmE_le_TSD`, `TSDmB_le_TSD`) whose mirror extension is divergence-free across the
faces, i.e. with the wall conditions `E_{τn} = 0`, `B_{nn} = 0` (weakly).

## Main results

* **`Feec.Models.Cube.Mirror.existsUnique_memQ`**: for `E₀ ∈ TSDmE`, `B₀ ∈ TSDmB` with `(0, E₀, B₀) ∈ D(L)`,
  (4.14) has a strong solution on `[0, T]`, unique among strong solutions, with `σ ≡ 0` and
  `E(t) ∈ TSDmE`, `B(t) ∈ TSDmB` for all `t`, and `(E, B)` solves (4.15).
* **`Feec.Models.Cube.Mirror.reducingSubcomplexQ`**: the projection hypothesis `P_K D(L) ⊆ D(L)` of Prop 4.17 holds.
* **`Feec.Models.Cube.Mirror.invariantCore_eqQ`**: `K* = K` for every orthogonal group generated by `-L`.
* **`Feec.Models.Cube.Mirror.exists_nonstationaryQ`**: the datum `(0, E₀, 0)`, `E₀ = 2 cos(2π x₃) diag(1, -1, 0)`
  on `Q`, lies in `D(L) ∩ K` and is not stationary for any such group (contrast
  `Feec.Legacy.BoxIdent.thesisComplexQ_mem_Kmax_iff'` for the thesis' boundary conditions).

## Scope

The box is `Q = (0, ½)³`; every open cube, e.g. the unit cube `(0, 1)³` meshed in Ch. 7, is its
image under `x ↦ 2s x + b`, and the transport is `Feec.Legacy.MirrorCube.Pi`. The Ch. 7 test solution
itself (a plane wave whose boundary values are non-zero and time-dependent) satisfies no
homogeneous boundary condition and is not an instance of this repair. Curved domains are not
treated: on a curved boundary `σ · n = 0` does not give `(∇σ)_{nτ} = 0` (second fundamental form),
so these conditions do not form a complex there (analysis, not formalized).

## References

* [QuennevilleBelair2015], §4.10 (Prop 4.17, (4.14), (4.15))
* [AFW2010] (Hilbert complexes)
* [Brezis2011], §9.2 (extension by reflection)
-/

@[expose] public noncomputable section

open scoped RealInnerProductSpace InnerProductSpace ComplexConjugate
open MeasureTheory Set Filter Topology LinearPMap

namespace Feec.Legacy.MirrorCube

open Feec.Legacy.Torus Feec.Legacy.TorusWeak Feec.Legacy.Box Feec.Legacy.BoxIdent Feec.Legacy.Constraints Feec.Legacy.HilbertComplex2
open Feec.Legacy.BoundedDomain (R3 Ix IsTest curlM)

/-- The partial derivative of `Feec.Legacy.BoundedDomain`. -/
local notation "pd" => Feec.Legacy.BoundedDomain.pd

/-- `L²(Q; ℝ³)`. -/
abbrev VQ := BoundedDomain.L2V Qr
/-- `L²(Q; ℝ³ˣ³)`. -/
abbrev MQ := BoundedDomain.L2M Qr

/-- **The Hilbert complex of the box with tensorial mirror boundary conditions**,
`H¹_n(Q; ℝ³) --grad--> H_{nτ}(curl, Q; ℝ³ˣ³) --curl--> L²(Q; ℝ³ˣ³)` (`σ · n = 0`, `E_{nτ} = 0`),
as the compression of the periodic complex by the mirror extensions. -/
def mirrorCxQ : HilbertComplex2 VQ MQ MQ :=
  comprComplex periodicComplex comprV (comprM 1 one_mul_one) (comprM (-1) neg_one_mul_neg_one)
    comprComm_grad comprComm_curl

/-- The electric constraint space: TSD fields on `Q` whose mirror (tensor) extension is TSD on
`𝕋³` (wall condition `E_{τn} = 0`). -/
abbrev TSDmE : Submodule ℝ MQ := L2TSD.comap ((comprM 1 one_mul_one).J : MQ →ₗ[ℝ] L2M)

/-- The magnetic constraint space: TSD fields on `Q` whose mirror (pseudo-tensor) extension is TSD
on `𝕋³` (wall condition `B_{nn} = 0`). -/
abbrev TSDmB : Submodule ℝ MQ := L2TSD.comap ((comprM (-1) neg_one_mul_neg_one).J : MQ →ₗ[ℝ] L2M)

theorem eight_pos : (0 : ℝ) < 8 := by norm_num

/-! ## The domains and the operators are the weak derivatives on `Q` -/

section Faithful

theorem mem_d0_domain {σ : VQ} : σ ∈ mirrorCxQ.d0.domain ↔ Jv σ ∈ gradT.domain := Iff.rfl

theorem mem_d1_domain {E : MQ} : E ∈ mirrorCxQ.d1.domain ↔ Jm 1 one_mul_one E ∈ Hcurl := Iff.rfl

/-- `d0 σ = (grad Jv σ)|_Q`. -/
theorem mirrorCxQ_d0_apply (σ : mirrorCxQ.d0.domain) :
    mirrorCxQ.d0 σ = resB (gradT ⟨Jv σ, σ.2⟩) := rfl

/-- `d1 E = (curl Jm₁ E)|_Q`. -/
theorem mirrorCxQ_d1_apply (E : mirrorCxQ.d1.domain) :
    mirrorCxQ.d1 E = resB (curlT ⟨Jm 1 one_mul_one E, E.2⟩) := rfl

/-- **`d0` is the weak gradient on `Q`**: `∫_Q σ_a ∂_b φ = -∫_Q (d0 σ)_{ab} φ` for
`φ ∈ C_c^∞(Q)`. -/
theorem mirrorCxQ_d0_weakGrad (σ : mirrorCxQ.d0.domain) (a b : Fin 3) {φ : R3 → ℝ}
    (hφ : IsTest Qr φ) :
    ∫ x, (σ : VQ) a x * pd b φ x ∂volume.restrict Qr =
      -∫ x, mirrorCxQ.d0 σ (a, b) x * φ x ∂volume.restrict Qr := by
  have hw : IsWeakGrad (vectorFourier.symm (Jv σ)) (matrixFourier.symm (gradT ⟨Jv σ, σ.2⟩)) :=
    (isWeakGrad_iff _ _).2 fun k => by
      simp only [LinearIsometryEquiv.apply_symm_apply]
      rfl
  have h := resV_weakGrad hw a b hφ
  have e : resV (vectorFourier.symm (Jv σ)) = (σ : VQ) := resBV_Jv σ
  rw [e] at h
  exact h

/-- **`d1` is the weak curl on `Q`**: `D(d1) ⊆ H(curl, Q)` (the domain of the maximal curl
`d1*` of the thesis' complex on `Q`) and `d1 E` is the weak curl of `E`. -/
theorem mirrorCxQ_d1_eq (E : mirrorCxQ.d1.domain) :
    ∃ h : (E : MQ) ∈ cxQ.d1†.domain, cxQ.d1† ⟨E, h⟩ = mirrorCxQ.d1 E := by
  obtain ⟨h, e⟩ := resB_curl (A := Jm 1 one_mul_one E) E.2
  rw [resB_Jm] at h
  refine ⟨h, ?_⟩
  rw [mirrorCxQ_d1_apply, ← e]
  exact lpmap_congr' _ _ _ (resB_Jm _ _ _).symm

theorem mirrorCxQ_d1_domain_le {E : MQ} (hE : E ∈ mirrorCxQ.d1.domain) :
    E ∈ BoundedDomain.HcurlM Qr :=
  (BoundedDomain.thesisComplex_adjoint_d1_iff isOpen_Qr isBounded_Qr).1
    (mirrorCxQ_d1_eq ⟨E, hE⟩).1

/-- **`d1*` is the weak curl on `Q`.** -/
theorem mirrorCxQ_adj1_eq (B : mirrorCxQ.d1†.domain) :
    ∃ h : (B : MQ) ∈ cxQ.d1†.domain, cxQ.d1† ⟨B, h⟩ = mirrorCxQ.d1† B := by
  have hJ : (comprM (-1) neg_one_mul_neg_one).J B ∈ periodicComplex.d1†.domain :=
    (mem_adj1_compr_iff (h0 := comprComm_grad) (h1 := comprComm_curl) eight_pos).1 B.2
  have hJc : Jm (-1) neg_one_mul_neg_one B ∈ Hcurl := by
    have := hJ; change _ ∈ curlT†.domain at this; rwa [adjoint_curlT] at this
  have e1 := J_adjoint_compr comprComm_curl periodicComplex.dense1 B hJ
  have e2 : periodicComplex.d1† ⟨_, hJ⟩ = curlT ⟨_, hJc⟩ := by
    change curlT† ⟨_, hJ⟩ = curlT ⟨_, hJc⟩
    have : ∀ (T T' : L2M →ₗ.[ℝ] L2M) (h : T = T') (x : L2M) (hx : x ∈ T.domain)
        (hx' : x ∈ T'.domain), T ⟨x, hx⟩ = T' ⟨x, hx'⟩ := by
      intro T T' h x hx hx'; subst h; rfl
    exact this _ _ adjoint_curlT _ _ _
  obtain ⟨h, e⟩ := resB_curl hJc
  rw [show resB (Jm (-1) neg_one_mul_neg_one B) = B from resB_Jm _ _ _] at h
  refine ⟨h, ?_⟩
  have e3 : mirrorCxQ.d1† B = resB (curlT ⟨_, hJc⟩) := by
    rw [← e2, ← e1]; exact (resB_Jm _ _ _).symm
  rw [e3, ← e]
  exact lpmap_congr' _ _ _ (resB_Jm _ _ _).symm

/-- **`d0*` is the weak `-div` on `Q`.** -/
theorem mirrorCxQ_adj0_eq (E : mirrorCxQ.d0†.domain) :
    ∃ h : (E : MQ) ∈ cxQ.d0†.domain, cxQ.d0† ⟨E, h⟩ = mirrorCxQ.d0† E := by
  have hJ : (comprM 1 one_mul_one).J E ∈ periodicComplex.d0†.domain :=
    (mem_adjoint_compr_iff comprComm_grad periodicComplex.dense0 eight_pos).1 E.2
  have hJd : Jm 1 one_mul_one E ∈ Hdiv := by
    have := hJ; change _ ∈ gradT†.domain at this; rwa [adjoint_gradT_domain] at this
  have e1 := J_adjoint_compr comprComm_grad periodicComplex.dense0 E hJ
  have e2 : periodicComplex.d0† ⟨_, hJ⟩ = -TorusWeak.divT ⟨_, hJd⟩ := by
    refine lp.ext (funext fun k => ?_)
    have h := adjoint_mulOp_apply (fun k => gradSym (freq k)) ⟨_, hJ⟩ k
    rw [adjoint_gradSym] at h
    exact h.trans (by rw [lp.coeFn_neg, Pi.neg_apply]; rfl)
  obtain ⟨h, e⟩ := resB_div hJd
  rw [show resB (Jm 1 one_mul_one E) = E from resB_Jm _ _ _] at h
  refine ⟨h, ?_⟩
  have e3 : mirrorCxQ.d0† E = -resBV (TorusWeak.divT ⟨_, hJd⟩) := by
    rw [← _root_.map_neg, ← e2, ← e1]; exact (resBV_Jv _).symm
  rw [e3, ← e]
  exact lpmap_congr' _ _ _ (resB_Jm _ _ _).symm

/-- The restriction of a periodic `L²(TSD)` field is in `L²(TSD)(Q)`. -/
theorem resB_mem_TSD_of_L2TSD {A : L2M} (hA : A ∈ L2TSD) : resB A ∈ BoundedDomain.TSD Qr := by
  refine ⟨fun i j => ?_, ?_, fun φ hφ => ?_⟩
  · rw [resB_apply, resB_apply]
    congr 2
    ext k
    exact (hA k).1 i j
  · simp only [resB_apply, ← map_sum, ← ofCoeff_sum]
    have : (∑ i, entry (i, i) A) = 0 := by
      ext k
      simp only [lp.coeFn_sum, Finset.sum_apply, entry_apply, lp.coeFn_zero, Pi.zero_apply]
      exact (hA k).2.1
    rw [this]
    simp [ofCoeff]
  · have hd : A ∈ Hdiv := L2TSD_le_Hdiv hA
    have hw : IsWeakDiv (matrixFourier.symm A) (vectorFourier.symm (TorusWeak.divT ⟨A, hd⟩)) :=
      (isWeakDiv_iff _ _).2 fun k => by
        simp only [LinearIsometryEquiv.apply_symm_apply]
        rfl
    have h := resM_weakDiv hw hφ
    have h0 : TorusWeak.divT ⟨A, hd⟩ = 0 := by
      refine lp.ext (funext fun k => ?_)
      change divSym (freq k) (A k) = 0
      ext a
      simp [divSym_apply, (hA k).2.2 a]
    rw [h0, _root_.map_zero, _root_.map_zero] at h
    refine h.trans ?_
    rw [neg_eq_zero]
    refine Finset.sum_eq_zero fun i _ => integral_eq_zero_of_ae ?_
    filter_upwards [Lp.coeFn_zero ℝ 2 (volume.restrict Qr)] with x hx
    change ((0 : BoundedDomain.L2 Qr) : R3 → ℝ) x * φ i x = 0
    rw [hx]; simp

/-- **The electric constraint space consists of TSD fields on `Q`.** -/
theorem TSDmE_le_TSD : TSDmE ≤ BoundedDomain.TSD Qr := fun E hE => by
  have h : Jm 1 one_mul_one E ∈ L2TSD := hE
  have := resB_mem_TSD_of_L2TSD h
  rwa [resB_Jm] at this

/-- **The magnetic constraint space consists of TSD fields on `Q`.** -/
theorem TSDmB_le_TSD : TSDmB ≤ BoundedDomain.TSD Qr := fun B hB => by
  have h : Jm (-1) neg_one_mul_neg_one B ∈ L2TSD := hB
  have := resB_mem_TSD_of_L2TSD h
  rwa [resB_Jm] at this

end Faithful

/-! ## A non-stationary TSD datum -/

section Nonstationary

theorem neg_k0_or (k : Z3) : (-k = k0 ∨ -k = -k0) ↔ (k = k0 ∨ k = -k0) := by
  constructor
  · rintro (h | h)
    · right; rw [← h, neg_neg]
    · left; exact neg_inj.1 h
  · rintro (h | h)
    · right; rw [h]
    · left; rw [h, neg_neg]

theorem isRealM_cosE : IsRealM cosE := fun k p => by
  change cosField (-k) p = conj (cosField k p)
  unfold cosField
  simp only [neg_k0_or]
  split_ifs
  · obtain ⟨a, b⟩ := p
    simp only [M0, mat_apply]
    split_ifs <;> simp
  · simp

/-- The electric datum `E₀ = (2 cos(2π x₃) diag(1, -1, 0))|_Q`. -/
def cosEQ : MQ := resB cosE

theorem Jm_cosEQ : Jm 1 one_mul_one cosEQ = cosE := Jm_resB one_mul_one cosE_mem_fix isRealM_cosE

theorem cosEQ_mem_TSDmE : cosEQ ∈ TSDmE := by
  change Jm 1 one_mul_one cosEQ ∈ L2TSD
  rw [Jm_cosEQ]; exact cosE_mem_L2TSD

theorem cosEQ_mem_TSD : cosEQ ∈ BoundedDomain.TSD Qr := TSDmE_le_TSD cosEQ_mem_TSDmE

/-- The datum `(0, E₀, 0)`. -/
def cosStateQ : Tot VQ MQ MQ := ini VQ cosEQ 0

theorem cosStateQ_mem_Kc : cosStateQ ∈ Kc VQ TSDmE TSDmB := by
  rw [mem_Kc, cosStateQ, tot_ini]
  exact ⟨rfl, cosEQ_mem_TSDmE, TSDmB.zero_mem⟩

theorem tot_totJ_cosStateQ :
    tot L2V L2M L2M (totJ comprV (comprM 1 one_mul_one) (comprM (-1) neg_one_mul_neg_one)
      cosStateQ) = (0, cosE, 0) := by
  rw [tot_totJ, cosStateQ, tot_ini]
  simp only [_root_.map_zero]
  exact Prod.ext rfl (Prod.ext Jm_cosEQ rfl)

/-- `(0, E₀, 0) ∈ D(L)`. -/
theorem cosStateQ_mem_domL : cosStateQ ∈ mirrorCxQ.domL := by
  rw [mirrorCxQ, mem_domL_compr_iff eight_pos, Constraints.mem_domL, tot_totJ_cosStateQ]
  refine ⟨periodicComplex.d0.domain.zero_mem, ⟨cosE_mem_Hcurl, ?_⟩,
    periodicComplex.d1†.domain.zero_mem⟩
  exact (LinearPMap.mem_ker_iff.1 (L2TSD_le_ker cosE_mem_L2TSD)).elim fun y hy => hy.1 ▸ y.2

/-- `L (0, E₀, 0) ≠ 0`: the `B`-component of its extension is `-curl (cos field) ≠ 0`. -/
theorem cosStateQ_waveOp_ne :
    mirrorCxQ.waveOp ⟨cosStateQ, cosStateQ_mem_domL⟩ ≠ 0 := by
  intro h0
  have hi := totJ_waveOp (h0 := comprComm_grad) (h1 := comprComm_curl) eight_pos cosStateQ
    cosStateQ_mem_domL
  change totJ _ _ _ (mirrorCxQ.waveOp ⟨cosStateQ, cosStateQ_mem_domL⟩) = _ at hi
  rw [h0, _root_.map_zero] at hi
  have h3 := congrArg (fun y => (tot L2V L2M L2M y).2.2 k0) hi
  simp only [Constraints.tot_waveOp, _root_.map_zero, Prod.snd_zero, lp.coeFn_zero,
    Pi.zero_apply] at h3
  rw [lp.coeFn_neg, Pi.neg_apply, eq_comm, neg_eq_zero] at h3
  apply curlSym_cosE_ne
  rw [← h3]
  change curlSym (freq k0) (cosE k0) = curlSym (freq k0)
    ((tot L2V L2M L2M (totJ comprV (comprM 1 one_mul_one) (comprM (-1) neg_one_mul_neg_one)
      cosStateQ)).2.1 k0)
  rw [tot_totJ_cosStateQ]

end Nonstationary

end Feec.Legacy.MirrorCube
